! ja_ua1_ssip "SSIP", the SIP17 indicator-reset chain, PDF pp.17-18
! (octal 001572.00-001604.40).  "RESET INDICATORS".
!
! FIRST TRANSCRIPTION FROM THIS TAPE.  ja_ua1_ssip is the System Test
! Program's supervisor; its listing is PDF pp.7-52 (1-up fanfold, no
! printed page numbers, so cite by PDF page).
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK.  It walks indicators 0 through 19 IN NUMERIC ORDER,
! one BRANCH-ON-INDICATOR-AND-CLEAR each, then sweeps the rest with a
! single SX into word 11.  That makes it a self-checking table of two
! things at once: the indicator NUMBERING for bits 0-19, and the
! branch-on-indicator ENCODING rule.  If either is wrong anywhere in
! that range, exactly one row's machine code disagrees -- twenty
! independent checks in twenty-two half-words.
!
! IT ALSO REACHES THE INDICATORS NOTHING ELSE DOES.  OP (15), AD (16),
! USA (17), EXE (18) and DS (19) are the instruction-exception group;
! op_ad_indicators.strap pins OP and AD by hand from the manual, and
! this is a DECK naming all five.
!
! TWO THINGS THE LISTING SETTLES.
!
! SLOT 14 IS NOT AN INDICATOR.  Where every other row is a
! branch-on-indicator, 001601.00 is a plain "B,$.32" -- the chain steps
! over bit 14 with an ordinary branch because there is nothing there to
! test.  strap/opcodes.py's INDICATOR_BITS has always had a gap at 14;
! this is a second, independent witness to it, from a programmer who
! had the machine.
!
! THE DECKS SPELL INDICATOR 5 "CPU", not CPUS.  The Reference Manual's
! Figure 11 calls it "CPU Signal (CPUS)" and this project took CPUS
! from there.  SSIP writes BCPUZ.  Both are now in INDICATOR_BITS, as
! an alias, because the manual's name is what every comment here uses
! and the deck's name is what the listing needs.
!
! B,$.32 is written "B,$+.32" below: this assembler wants the explicit
! sign, and the assembled half-word is identical -- both branch to the
! next half-word, which is what the listing's 1601.50 00 encodes.

! External symbols, given by SYN at the addresses the listing prints.
! Rows that name one check the opcode and modifier bits only, since
! their address came from the same print -- listing_oracle's own
! convention.
RET1    SYN, (8)1307.0               ! the print/return entry
INT     SYN, (8)1353.0               ! the interrupt table origin
DSIP31  SYN, (8)2060.0               ! SSIP's mask constant
DSIP1   SYN, (8)2025.0               ! switches A and B
DSIP20  SYN, (8)2046.0               ! switch A
DSIP21  SYN, (8)2046.40              ! switch B -- same word, second half
DSIP22  SYN, (8)2047.0               ! switch C
!
! ---- SIP16: reset the interrupt system's own control state --------
! This is the block that writes the PERMANENTLY PROTECTED area.  p.31:
! "Locations 1, 2, and 3 are referred to as the permanently protected
! area of storage.  References to these locations always give an
! address monitoring signal, regardless of the contents of the boundary
! registers or the setting of the boundary control bit."  Words 1, 2
! and 3 are the interval timer, the interruption address register and
! the boundary registers -- the interrupt system protecting its own
! control state.
!
! AND THE DECK DISABLES INTERRUPTS BEFORE TOUCHING IT.  A BD guarded
! this sequence, commented "DISABLE BEFORE RESET OF PROTECTED AREA",
! which is the deck's own witness for what p.45 states: DS/DF/IF are
! raised only "while the interruption system was enabled".  A program
! that needs to rewrite the protected area turns the system off first.
! When storage protection is implemented here, this block is the
! natural test -- it must succeed disabled and be suppressed enabled.
        SLC, (8)1563.40
! THE LABEL SITS ON THE BXVLZ, NOT ON THE CHAIN.  The first version of
! this program put SIP17 on the BMKZ at 001572.00, which is wrong: the
! listing labels the BXVLZ two half-words earlier.  Caught by reading
! further up the page while scouting the next block -- the sort of
! error a verify script cannot find, because it checks the address a
! symbol resolves to, and a symbol on the wrong row still resolves to
! something.
        SV, $X13, 1.0                ! reset interval timer      (word 1, P)
        LX, $X13, DSIP31             ! SSIP's mask constant
        SX, $X13, 12.0               ! reset mask                (word 12)
SIP16   LX, $X13, 0.0                ! X13 := the protected zero
        SX, $X13, 3.0                ! reset boundaries and control bit
                                     !                           (word 3, P)
        LVI, $X13, INT               ! the interrupt table origin
        SV, $X13, 2.0                ! reset interrupt address   (word 2, P)
        LV, $X13, DSIP1              ! reset switches A and B
        SV, $X13, DSIP20
        SV, $X13, DSIP21
        LV, $X13, DSIP22             ! test that switch C is not on
SIP17   BXVLZ, $                     ! * error made in SSIP -- hang if set
        LX, $X13, 0.0                ! X13 := the protected zero, for the
                                     !   SX that sweeps the rest below
        BMKZ, $+.32                  ! 0  machine check
        BIKZ, $+.32                  ! 1  instruction check   -RESET INDICATORS
        BIJZ, $+.32                  ! 2  instruction reject
        BEKZ, $+.32                  ! 3  exchange check
        BTSZ, $+.32                  ! 4  time signal
        BCPUZ, $+.32                 ! 5  CPU signal  (deck spelling: CPU)
        BEKJZ, $+.32                 ! 6  exchange check reject
        BUNRJZ, $+.32                ! 7  unit not ready reject
        BCBJZ, $+.32                 ! 8  channel busy reject
        BEPGKZ, $+.32                ! 9  exchange program check
        BUKZ, $+.32                  ! 10 unit check
        BEEZ, $+.32                  ! 11 end exception
        BEOPZ, $+.32                 ! 12 end of operation
        BCSZ, $+.32                  ! 13 channel signal
        B, $+.32                     ! 14 RESERVED -- a plain branch
        BOPZ, $+.32                  ! 15 operation code invalid
        BADZ, $+.32                  ! 16 address invalid
        BUSAZ, $+.32                 ! 17 unended sequence of addresses
        BEXEZ, $+.32                 ! 18 execute exception
        BDSZ, $+.32                  ! 19 data store
        SX, $X13, 11.0               ! reset rest of ind.
        B, RET1                      ! back to the caller
        END, SIP17
